Embedded React: size the main axis from a definite cross size and aspectRatio.

Modified from Embedded React (Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 Cory Lamming) at the
revision pinned in dependencies.lock.json. Changed file: engine/layout/
layout_engine.c. Proposed upstream as pull request #305.

aspectRatio only derived a flow child's cross size from its main size. A child
whose cross size is definite (an explicit length or a percentage) and whose main
size is auto fell back to its content size instead, so an image in a row sized
`h-full aspect-[3/4]` was as wide as its bitmap: 0 until a remote image arrived,
then the bitmap's width. CSS and React Native derive the width from the height;
the main size now does the same, from the cross size after its min/max clamps.
Content measurement (an auto-sized parent sizing itself around such children)
applies the same rule to one explicit axis, so the parent and its laid-out
children agree. Children with a main size, a flex basis or no aspectRatio are
unchanged. Derived sizes saturate at the int16 range.

diff --git a/engine/layout/layout_engine.c b/engine/layout/layout_engine.c
--- a/engine/layout/layout_engine.c
+++ b/engine/layout/layout_engine.c
@@ -425,6 +425,12 @@
